[38;2;124;124;124mNow let me think about the problem.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$\mathcal{M}$ is the space of Lebesgue-measurable functions on $\mathbb{R}^n$. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mWhat topology does $\mathcal{M}$ carry? This is the key question. The space of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmeasurable functions is typically equipped with the topology of convergence in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmeasure (on sets of finite measure), or sometimes the metric $d(f,g) = \int [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\min(|f-g|, 1) / (1+|x|^n) dx$ or similar.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me think more carefully. The standard topology on $\mathcal{M}$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(the space of measurable functions, identified a.e.) is the topology of [0m
