[38;2;124;124;124mSo we need: $W^{k,2}$-Cauchy sequences in $C^\infty_c$ are $\mathcal{M}$-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mconvergent, and the $\mathcal{M}$-limit is determined by the $W^{k,2}$-limit.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is equivalent to: the $W^{k,2}$ topology on $C^\infty_c$ is finer than the [0m[38;2;124;124;124m$\mathcal{M}$ topology (i.e., $W^{k,2}$ convergence implies $\mathcal{M}$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mconvergence), AND the map is injective on the completion (i.e., if $u_j \to 0$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124min $W^{k,2}$, then $u_j \to 0$ in $\mathcal{M}$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, actually "extend by continuity" means: there exists a continuous linear [0m
